content.text:
Done. Implemented as approved, via TDD.

**`format.js`** — one new block, appended after `suffix` so the cap covers the composed string:

```js
if (typeof options.truncate === 'number' && result.length > options.truncate) {
  const max = options.truncate;

  if (max <= ELLIPSIS.length) {
    result = ELLIPSIS.slice(0, Math.max(0, max));
  } else {
    const candidate = result.slice(0, max - ELLIPSIS.length);
    const lastSpace = candidate.lastIndexOf(' ');
    const body = lastSpace > 0 ? candidate.slice(0, lastSpace) : candidate;
    result = body.trimEnd() + ELLIPSIS;
  }
}
```

No existing blocks were modified. `ELLIPSIS` is a module constant so the `max - 3` arithmetic and the literal can't drift apart.

**`format.test.js`** — 10 new `console.assert` lines in the existing style. No test runner added.

**Verification:** `node format.test.js` → all 15 assertions pass, zero `Assertion failed` on stderr, exit 0. I watched 8 of the 10 new tests fail first for the right reason; the two passthrough tests (under-cap, exactly-at-cap) passed from the start since unchanged input is the correct answer there — they're regression guards against a boundary off-by-one, not tests I proved can fail.

Two things worth flagging:

- **The Codex approach gate didn't contribute.** Preflight reported `ok`, but the installed Codex is a stub (`0.0.0-stub`) and the call returned an empty payload. One shot, no retry per the gate, so the exact-cut vs word-boundary reasoning was mine alone with no independent check.
- **The aggressive-backoff case is live, as agreed.** `format("a verylongwordhere", { truncate: 12 })` returns `"a..."` — the backoff hits the space at index 1 and discards nearly everything. You accepted the design with this known; say the word and I'll add the half-window floor.

Pre-existing and untouched: `node` prints a `MODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON` warning because `package.json` lacks `"type": "module"`. Adding it would break `src/utils.js`/`src/index.js`, which are CommonJS — out of scope here.

Changes are in the working tree on `feature/add-truncate`, uncommitted.
